WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.000
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.080
Where's dad?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.530
He went to the Family Court.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.080
He is expected home shortly.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.170
There's no way mom did anything wrong.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.760
That's true.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.010
But you can't just blame dad.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.770
Because neither side is completely wrong.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.870
But...

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.510
I have a favor to ask you.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.620
Sure!

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.900
Let's not tell dad about this conversation.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.010
Why?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.410
Because it would hurt dad.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.920
You don't want that to happen, right?

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.610
So, that is the favor I ask of you.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.480
Sure!

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.890
Masakazu, there's a problem.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.810
Seems it's broken.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.570
Good morning,Tex.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.870
Tex...

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.320
Hey, Tex!

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.290
Tex!

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.310
Time of Eve

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.840
The future, probably Japan.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.250
Robots have long been in use,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.720
And practical use of androids has just begun.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.660
Next, the report from the preliminary investigation.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.880
This shows the places that

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:05.480
seem to be inciting excessive human-robot interactions.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.090
There's too many.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.390
1408 places.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.920
We gathered all possible information

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.780
and codified all of it.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.360
Groundless rumors and urban legends included.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.300
We need to narrow it down.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:25.160
Unfortunately, all these places don't clearly violate robot law.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.650
It's a grey zone.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.350
And the fact that there are so many of these places

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.500
shows the limitations to robot law as it stands now.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.660
But, these places must be eliminated.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.540
We'll do a cursory investigation of all the places,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.180
and then pick targets for full investigation.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.370
After that, hand them over to the media.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.890
But it's impossible given the sheer number!

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.480
That's true, in terms of manpower...

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.050
For the first time ever,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.530
we'll use androids for the cursory investigation.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.600
We've already secured a large number -

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.710
We're getting them ready now.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.050
What happened to your allergy to robots?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.470
Fight poison with poison.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.010
I suggest you think of it like that.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:11.600
Continue.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.490
We'll only fully investigate the places

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.510
substantiated by the android investigations.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:24.300
And, we'll record all androids and humans seen at the places.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.370
and we'll do follow-up investigations.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.200
We'll immediately report suspects

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.890
to committee members who are in the police force

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.360
and urge them to make arrests.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.610
What's happening with the Android Promotion Committee?

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.550
Someone has sniffed out the preliminary investigation.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.690
Their relationship with the APC is unclear.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:44.300
Also, lobbying has quieted down.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.800
So, don't forget that some parties

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.910
will try using this investigation to trip us up.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.240
We will order the android investigators

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.690
to keep their ties with our committee absolutely secret.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.540
Memories of that injury incident are fading.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.970
We must not make the same mistake again.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.690
Go on.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.140
Media strategy division.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.140
CIO Masaki will make a TV appearance -

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.400
My wife records them all.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.010
Drives me nuts!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.760
<i>I'd like to emphasize</i>

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.020
<i>that our Ethics Committee is raising the alarm about</i>

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:31.020
<i>robots infiltrating into daily life, that's all.</i>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.240
Woah! What a lady killer!

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.980
Huh? How?

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.650
Hey, you changed the channel!

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.070
Thanks for letting me stop by!

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.800
<i>Children treat robots like people -</i>

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.290
<i>no matter how primitive the robots are.</i>

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.860
<i>And that impedes the relationships</i>

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.800
<i>that we're supposed to have between humans.</i>

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.050
One Evelend!

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.240
Sure.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.720
<i>...it's an encroachment on human dignity.</i>

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.230
<i>The issue I'm raising here is -</i>

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.850
Hey, why doesn't Masaki come anymore?

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.730
Actually, a lot has happened...

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.250
Like what?!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.120
Well, the biggest reason is...

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.070
This guy is on TV a lot these days, huh?

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.400
Yeah. Like the old days...

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:11.610
What's this?

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.660
The Robot Ethics Committee has been around

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.810
since androids started being used in households.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.910
More than 10 years.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.920
I've heard that it started out

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.120
as a radical anti-robot organization.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.620
I had no idea.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.040
'Cause they've been quiet for the last few years.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.450
What do you mean?

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:34.110
Their radicalness led to an injury.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:37.040
The Tokisaka Incident, right?

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.730
I've heard of it.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.720
...it's also referred to as an accident.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.630
At any rate, they were severely censured

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.460
and the head resigned.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:47.860
Since then,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.760
they've been quiet, at least until recently.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.110
You've lost me...

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.980
Does it have anything to do with Masaki?

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.810
<i>...that is our stance.</i>

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.520
<i>Thank you very much, Mr. Masaki.</i>

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.690
<i>Today's guest for Zoom-in Scramble has been</i>

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:08.850
<i>Atsuro Masaki, Chief Information Officer of the Ethics Committee.</i>

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.510
Masaki...

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:14.000
That's right...his family circumstances..

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.380
I invited him today too -

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.140
So Masaki is his last name.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.230
You're hung up on that...?

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.290
Not that!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.580
Eve's Friendships

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.530
So, how's it going?

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.920
There's this cafe called Time of Eve,

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:42.950
Rikuo's a big fan.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.620
I go there too, so who am I to talk.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.610
Humans and androids talk to each other!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.350
It's totally absurd.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.720
Yeah?

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:04.800
Say something.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:05.940
I'm coming in.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.860
Who're you talking to?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.020
My mobile phone.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.240
I hung up already.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.300
You had it make coffee?

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:15.830
Yeah.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.210
You're at home a lot these days.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.650
Did something happen?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.720
Tell me everything.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.950
There's nothing.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:29.680
Oh, I see.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.640
Don't trust robots too much

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.760
when it comes to things you eat and drink.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.800
THX, tonight we'll write up the minutes from today's meeting.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.930
The data is in my terminal.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.120
Tell Masaki he's welcome anytime.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:50.920
Sure, I'll tell him.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.600
But don't get your hopes up.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.600
See you.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.750
Come again!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.200
Um, he's gone...

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.700
You know, I don't think Rikuo minds anymore.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.210
That's the impression I get.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.410
Nagi, you don't understand Rikuo.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.210
I've known him longer.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.780
I'm sure he doesn't want to see me here yet.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:16.970
Really?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.750
Hey, who cares about Rikuo?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.070
Of course we care about Rikuo!

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.590
Oh...really?!

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.930
Don't go telling Rikuo strange things.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.240
Masaki's not going to report this place, is he...?

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.470
Meow.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.510
If that happens, this cafe will have to close.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.400
But it's such a wonderful place.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.560
Sammy,

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.250
do you remember how you first came here?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.820
I thought you invited me.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:06.430
I'm not able to bring anyone here.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.180
You probably learned about Time of Eve

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:13.230
from someone who'd been here.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:17.250
And Sammy, you brought Rikuo and Masaki.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:22.160
So if Masaki brings someone from the Ethics Committee,

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.030
there's nothing you can do about it.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.680
That's the end of these connections.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.800
And the end of this cafe.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:31.460
Nagi, that's OK with you?

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:36.550
In this cafe, everyone's hearts come together as one.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.260
I just want to see it through...

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:43.650
...how big can this circle grow?

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.900
Um, Master -

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.670
W-what?

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.330
Do you want Mr. Masaki to visit again...?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.180
...to the Time of Eve...

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.560
Yes, I'd like him to come again.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.930
Me too.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:14.060
OK, I'll definitely bring him tomorrow!

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:55.480
Masaki!

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.130
Today -

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:58.940
I'm not going.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.140
She said she wants you to come again.

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:05.190
Don't just say things.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.550
It's true!

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:07.830
Who?

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.610
Nagi, and -

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.020
Sammy said so too!

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.860
And that guy said he wants you to come too.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:21.030
They want me to come?

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.470
So what? It's a houseroid!

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:27.840
Right.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.120
That's right.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.910
You've changed.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.620
Masaki, what's going on?

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.440
You're just like I was, back then.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:47.060
You'll feel love, only to be betrayed later.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.990
It'd be better if that cafe didn't exist.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.720
That's it. It'd be better if it didn't exist.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.590
Dad! I want to talk to you about something!

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.910
The THX is gone.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.960
Masakazu, did you give it an order?

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:23.730
No...

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.780
It just went off...

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:26.870
It's completely broken.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.430
Gotta find it right away, and get rid of it.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:31.510
Get rid of it?

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:32.600
Of course!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.160
It's dealt with lots of Ethics Committee material.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:39.020
Gotta take care of it, before it becomes a headache!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.400
Masaki, I'm at Time of Eve. Can you help me?

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.320
What's that sound?

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:28.560
An ancient robot - an elderly customer - is here

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.580
It says to close the cafe!

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.960
I said, what is that sound?

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:33.430
The screen...

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:36.060
Anyway, it won't stop, whatever we say!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.290
And this THX model won't talk.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.840
Hey - what did you just say?

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.680
This cafe is the gray zone, right?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.510
Do something with that robot law of yours...

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:50.600
That was fast!

00:13:56.740 --> 00:14:00.410
<i>Close this establishment immediately.</i>

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.400
Tex, stop it.

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:07.160
T-Tex?

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:17.890
What are you doing here?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:30.040
Oh, so that's what this is about?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.910
You bring someone's robot,

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.110
and you want to make a scene, huh?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.160
I don't know how you brought it here,

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:41.710
You guys got Rikuo's robot to come here.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.570
You can do all kinds of things.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.650
This is a strange place, after all.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.440
Nagi didn't bring it here.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:48.210
Akiko...

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.690
You'll go that far to get me to come here.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.470
I'll tell you my story.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.750
It brought me up, long ago.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.100
It was my best friend.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.450
The one day, it suddenly stopped talking.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.110
I was a kid, and thought it was family.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.310
I felt hurt and betrayed.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.600
That's it. No big deal.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.320
There must be a reason why it didn't talk.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.140
I agree.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.920
It doesn't look so broken down.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:28.910
I know.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.820
I was 4 or 5 years old,

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.070
but I could guess what was going on.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.340
My dad ordered it to stop talking.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:39.360
Told it not to talk, no matter what happens.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.710
He tried to drive us apart.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.250
Just like something like my dad would do.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:45.330
Orders from parents get priority.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:48.170
Masaki, you're very perceptive.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.140
What's perceptive mean?

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.170
I didn't know that when I was a kid.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.420
I kept trying to talk with it.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.190
I begged forgiveness, in tears!

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:06.110
If commanded, it can ignore a crying, wailing child.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.030
For years.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:13.040
In the end -

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:16.520
They can't understand people's hearts!

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:30.000
<i>Use androids in the cursory investigation</i>

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.610
<i>This cafe called Time of Eve...I go there too...</i>

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:36.100
<i>Record all androids and humans...urge arrests.</i>

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.690
<i>...should be eliminated.</i>

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:49.790
<i>House rule: no discrimination between robots and humans</i>

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:01.300
I am going to b-break t-this cafe's rule.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:07.810
You are in violation of robot law 9, article 3.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:12.640
According to data in my possession, you are an android.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:15.490
If an android turns off its ring while in motion,

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.250
it is in violation of robot law.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:25.080
What's going on?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.190
Why is Tex speaking?

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.640
What about dad's command?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.030
A command...

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.390
It's breaking a command.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.110
Breaking the Second Law...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.060
...can only be for the First Law...

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.010
the First Law means...danger?

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:46.910
A human here is in danger...?

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.910
But...who does Tex know to be human?

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.420
Only me.

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:54.410
I'm in danger?

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.900
Tex is speaking...

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.540
to protect me?

00:17:58.560 --> 00:17:59.370
So,

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.280
it is necessary to take legal action

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.580
against your owner.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.700
I require information on your owner.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:14.230
<i>We order the android investigators to keep their ties with our committee absolutely secret.</i>

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.000
Masaki!

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.380
Masaki!

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.280
I'm not letting go!

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
I'm not letting go

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.300
until you talk to me.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.800
Tell me!

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.630
What were you thinking?

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.460
For so many years.

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:43.390
All that time.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:48.800
Watching me, all those years.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.850
You were right there with me.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:56.960
Tex, help me!

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.990
Speak to me!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:18.600
I couldn't speak to you...

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.420
I always wanted to be at your side...

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:28.420
I...

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.760
I...

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:36.940
...always...

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.730
Masakazu...

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:28.070
It wanted to protect you.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.960
I know that much.

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:35.880
It won't speak, once the danger has passed.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:39.190
It's still bound by dad's command.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:44.580
You wanted me to understand too, huh?

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:48.350
But, after all, I can't accept this.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:53.330
It might be impossible now,

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.690
but someday it will talk, for sure.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.930
Don't just say things.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.610
You're wrong.

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:02.370
It's not like I don't have a reason.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:03.810
But I can't express it well.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.730
I've seen so many things here.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:12.230
There's a lot of problems,

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.350
Each time it's distressing.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.280
But I feel like this is the right path.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.910
It's the same for you, Masaki.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:25.840
I'm sure...

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:39.300
You might be right.

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:48.370
I'll tell dad that I brought you out of the house.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:22:00.970
I...always...Masakazu...

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:06.720
Let's go home.

00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:31.910
How did it get in?

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:32.670
I held it.

00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:33.500
I lifted it up.

00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:36.260
You really are demanding a lot!

00:22:37.050 --> 00:22:40.350
Someday I'll get you to say thanks for today.

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:41.300
I love everyone.

00:22:43.050 --> 00:22:46.460
I'm so happy we can all be here.

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:55.450
They're going home together!

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:57.580
Hush!

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:09.380
Should I have helped them?

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:12.320
No, it's enough that you watched over them.

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:16.190
It might have turned into another dangerous incident.

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:23.200
I'm sure Shiotsuki understands that much.

00:23:23.430 --> 00:23:26.840
Indeed, Time of Eve's is rule #1138.

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.880
But he's not necessarily involved.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:36.830
An article about the Tokisaka Incident, from when it happened?

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.360
No - this is -

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:43.050
It's the real article, before the contents were replaced.

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:45.250
It says the victim was...

00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:50.350
...a minor...a little girl.

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:58.270
<i>Time of Eve - pending</i>

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:05.900
I forgot your Evelend today.

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:07.690
I thought something was missing.

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:11.640
How did Tex get to the cafe?

00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:13.120
You don't know?

00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:14.460
You know?

00:24:14.610 --> 00:24:16.410
I thought you were a regular here.

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:18.220
Rikuo, you've got a long way to go.

00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:20.070
Still a long way?

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:23.310
Huh? Someone new?

00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:25.320
I'm going to say hello.

00:24:25.490 --> 00:24:27.400
<i>This is my tale of the Time of Eve.</i>

00:24:27.450 --> 00:24:28.450
Welcome!

00:24:28.580 --> 00:24:29.780
Take a seat!

00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:32.100
I'll go take your order.

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:35.550
<i>Lots more happened to me, but</i>

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:38.860
You might not be here for long, but enjoy yourself!

00:24:39.060 --> 00:24:41.970
<i>But that's another story.</i>

00:24:42.680 --> 00:24:49.850
<i>Even if I can get everything I want</i>

00:24:50.060 --> 00:24:59.230
<i>Only your warmth is unreachable, untouchable</i>

00:24:59.340 --> 00:25:07.090
<i>Alone, under the cloudy sky</i>

00:25:08.510 --> 00:25:12.430
<i>Even when we want to look at each other,</i>

00:25:12.530 --> 00:25:16.770
<i>I end up averting my eyes</i>

00:25:16.900 --> 00:25:21.840
<i>We can't change language,</i>

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:25.980
<i>so within my heart</i>

00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:33.460
<i>I only want to watch over you always</i>

00:25:33.750 --> 00:25:39.010
<i>I want to rush up to right away and clasp</i>

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:42.870
<i>with that hand</i>

00:25:43.030 --> 00:25:50.040
<i>I embrace the tender time</i>

00:26:16.390 --> 00:26:20.320
<i>This moment I can share with you</i>

00:26:20.430 --> 00:26:25.060
<i>I believe that there is an eternity that can be stopped</i>

00:26:25.180 --> 00:26:29.760
<i>Your casual gestures</i>

00:26:29.850 --> 00:26:37.260
<i>set me off with palpitations and bewilderment</i>

00:26:38.070 --> 00:26:42.590
<i>On lonely nights,</i>

00:26:42.810 --> 00:26:47.480
<i>The melody I play over and over</i>

00:26:47.650 --> 00:26:51.410
<i>Cannot be heard by you</i>

00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:56.100
<i>but I want to present it to you</i>

00:26:56.300 --> 00:26:59.720
<i>Overflowing feelings,</i>

00:26:59.960 --> 00:27:02.740
<i>simply sent on the wind</i>

00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:06.800
I'm so tired.

00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:09.260
You really helped me today.

00:27:09.450 --> 00:27:11.330
It was my pleasure.

00:27:13.040 --> 00:27:14.900
Hey, come over for a sec.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.500
What is it?

00:27:17.130 --> 00:27:18.630
Bow your head.

00:27:19.090 --> 00:27:21.410
Like this...

00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:27.120
It looks good on you.

00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.510
Thank you...very much.

00:27:31.810 --> 00:27:36.860
Time of Eve - Directed by Yasuhiro YOSHIURA
